/*
  core/masks/share_behavior.spthy -- f_H for the SHARE action class, CEREMONY-AGNOSTIC (AGNOSTIC_MASKS.md).
  Collapses attentive_share / careless_share / busy_share. This is the most effect-heavy class: each
  outcome manifests as a different combination of Out / Oob facts using the step's payload <recip, pw>.
  So the BEHAVIOUR (which mask -> which outcome + the action facts Share / LeakPw / MisdeliveredPw) lives
  here, and a thin per-ceremony EFFECT ADAPTER (secure_email/protocol/share_effects.spthy) reads the
  generic ShareOutcome(P,rid,kind) + !StepData(P,rid,<recip,pw>) and produces the Out/Oob.

    Attentive ('oob')          : passphrase off the wire (the guide's rule).  -> Oob only
    Careless ('inband-leak')   : in-band leak; recipient still gets it (silent compromise). LeakPw. -> Out+Oob
    Busy ('misdeliver')        : fat-fingered to the wrong recipient; intended one locked out. MisdeliveredPw. -> Out

  RespMask(P,mask) gated by mask_state.spthy as before. The 'share' step is tagged for the agnostic
  detectors too (lexicon marks it Mental+Temporal demanding -> sigma1/sigma3; sigma2 is action-generic).
*/

rule Share_oob:
    [ !Step(P, rid, 'share'), !OutcomePolicy(mask, 'share', 'oob') ]
  --[ Share(P, mask), RespMask(P, mask), Answered(rid), ShareOOB(P, rid) ]->
    [ ShareOutcome(P, rid, 'oob') ]

rule Share_inband_leak:
    [ !Step(P, rid, 'share'), !OutcomePolicy(mask, 'share', 'inband-leak') ]
  --[ Share(P, mask), RespMask(P, mask), Answered(rid), LeakPw(P), Mask(P,'Attentive',mask) ]->
    [ ShareOutcome(P, rid, 'inband-leak') ]

rule Share_misdeliver:
    [ !Step(P, rid, 'share'), !OutcomePolicy(mask, 'share', 'misdeliver') ]
  --[ Share(P, mask), RespMask(P, mask), Answered(rid), MisdeliveredPw(P), Mask(P,'Attentive',mask) ]->
    [ ShareOutcome(P, rid, 'misdeliver') ]
